    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We have serum proteomics from 80 patients in our sepsis cohort and serum metabolomics from a separate group of 75 patients enrolled at another hospital; no patient is in both tables. I'd like DRAGON to build a partial-correlation network linking the proteins and metabolites."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like DRAGON to build a partial-correlation network linking the proteins and metabolites.\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set. DRAGON gives: one undirected partial-correlation network within and between two matched omics layers (any two, e.g. expression and methylation), across all samples. A p-value and a Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value for every edge (adjusted within each layer and across the layers), to filter edges by significance.\n\nI couldn't match this to a result any registered NetZoo workflow produces, so none is offered.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
